## Melova Android → backend URL

Copy this file to `local.properties` in the project root (same folder as `settings.gradle.kts`).

```properties
# Android Studio already has sdk.dir here — keep that line and add:
sdk.dir=/path/from/your/studio

# Pick ONE base URL for your setup:
#
# Android Emulator (default if omitted):
# melova.api.baseUrl=http://10.0.2.2:8000/
#
# Physical phone on same Wi‑Fi / iPhone hotspot (Mac is usually x.x.x.1):
melova.api.baseUrl=http://172.20.10.1:8000/
#
# USB debugging with port reverse (run: adb reverse tcp:8000 tcp:8000):
# melova.api.baseUrl=http://127.0.0.1:8000/
```

Find your Mac IP: System Settings → Network, or terminal: `ipconfig getifaddr en0`

After editing, **Rebuild** the app (Build → Rebuild Project).
